d11_hud: optional whip_core patch (whip_core-vehicle-stat-reading-d11).
Adds exports.whip_core:GetVehicleStatReading(name, { entity = veh }): this client's live gauge reading for a vehicle stat,
the number whip_core's own capsule draws (whip_autos' turbo boost and nitrous for the driver). Read only.
Made on whip_core 1.0.1; applies to 1.1.0. From resources/: patch -p1 < whip_core-vehicle-stat-reading-d11.patch
This patch changes whip_core and is under whip_core's license (LGPL-3.0).

--- a/whip_core/client/vehicles.lua
+++ b/whip_core/client/vehicles.lua
@@ -296,6 +296,18 @@
     return tonumber(value)
 end
 
+--- This client's gauge reading for a stat on a car, as its own capsule draws it: a watcher's live reading (what its
+--- whileHeld last returned, e.g. whip_autos' boost and nitro for the driver), else the SetVehicleStatDisplay provider,
+--- else nil. Read only, for HUD resources that draw the gauge themselves (d11_hud). Patch: whip_core-vehicle-stat-reading-d11.
+---@param name string
+---@param vehicle WhipVehicleRef  `{ entity = veh }`
+---@return number|nil
+exports('GetVehicleStatReading', function(name, vehicle)
+    local entity = type(vehicle) == 'table' and tonumber(vehicle.entity) or nil
+    if type(name) ~= 'string' or not entity or not DoesEntityExist(entity) then return nil end
+    return readVehicleStatDisplay(name, entity, nil)
+end)
+
 --- Whether a stat's gauge is drawn on a car, by a resource's rule (SetVehicleStatShown), e.g. no fuel gauge on an
 --- electric car. [statName] = { fn = function(entity) -> false to hide }.
 local _statShown = {}
